  "body": "Majestic, iconic, bespoke, imposing, substantial, and historically significant. These are all terms that spring readily to mind when describing a Devonport Mansion that is undoubtedly one of a kind.\r\n\r\nMargaret House rests on a flat and sunny 1443 m2 freehold site. The main residence has 6 bedrooms, 4 bathrooms, 2 expansive formal lounge areas, a superb modern kitchen, 2 offices, and a separate laundry. There are also a 2-car garage and a separate 1 car garage.\r\n\r\nOn the East side of this massive plot, you will find a large studio with kitchenette and en-suite bathroom, plus an outdoor boat parking space to the side.\r\n\r\nThe magnificent gardens, which you enter through secure electric gates, envelops the beautiful buildings within, and on the sunny west side, there is an elevated entertaining deck with adjacent 11,000 litres Vortex swim/spa pool.\r\n\r\nHistorically, Margaret House was originally built in 1903-4 for Frederick Prime J.P., the founder of an Auckland hardware company. In 1953-4, it was purchased by the Navy as an additional hostel and named Margaret House. It provided accommodation for both Chief Petty Officers and Petty Officer Service Women until the 1970’s.\r\n\r\nIn November 2009, the Law Family purchased Margaret House and have spent many years lovingly restoring this unique and special residence, uncovering her rich history and stately presence. They have succeeded in transforming her into a meticulously presented, warm, dry and healthy home.\r\n\r\nThis majestic beauty has featured in the ‘Fine Homes Tour of Devonport’ and now awaits its proud new owners.",
